  "instructions": [
    {
      "section": "Preparation",
      "text": "Read the entire method first and measure the following ingredients before turning on the heat: 1 can (29 ounces) tomato puree; 1-1/2 cups plain yogurt; 1/2 large onion, finely chopped; 2 tablespoons olive oil; 4-1/2 teaspoons minced fresh gingerroot; 4 garlic cloves, minced; 1 tablespoon garam masala; 2-1/2 teaspoons salt; 1-1/2 teaspoons ground cumin; 1 teaspoon paprika; 3/4 teaspoon pepper; 1/2 teaspoon cayenne pepper; 1/4 teaspoon ground cinnamon; 2-1/2 pounds boneless skinless chicken breasts, cut into 1-1/2-inch cubes; 1 jalapeno pepper, halved and seeded; 1 bay leaf; 1 tablespoon cornstarch; 1 cup heavy whipping cream; Hot cooked basmati rice; Chopped fresh cilantro, optional. Keep ingredients marked optional separate until their step."
    },
    {
      "section": "Preparation",
      "text": "Prepare these ingredients before cooking: Onion: large; finely chopped; Gingerroot: minced fresh; Garlic: minced; Boneless skinless chicken breasts: cut into 1 1/2-inch cubes; Cilantro, optional: Chopped fresh. Wash produce under running water before cutting. Use a cutting board and a sharp knife; keep raw meat and its utensils separate from ready-to-eat ingredients."
    },
    {
      "text": "In a 5-qt. slow cooker, combine the first 13 ingredients (Can blend these first for convenience).",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Add chicken, jalapeno and bay leaf.",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook, covered, on low 4 hours or until chicken is tender.",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove jalapeno and bay leaf.",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "text": "In a small bowl, mix cornstarch and cream until smooth; gradually stir into sauce.",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook, covered, on high 15-20 minutes or until sauce is thickened.",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "section": "Check doneness",
      "text": "Before serving, insert a food thermometer into the thickest piece of chicken or turkey, away from bone: it must reach 165°F (74°C). If using already-cooked poultry, reheat it to 165°F (74°C). Continue cooking and recheck if needed; wash hands and utensils after handling raw poultry and do not rinse it."
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve with rice.",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "text": "If desired, sprinkle with cilantro.",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "section": "Finish",
      "text": "Turn off any burners or oven when cooking is finished. Follow the cooling or resting instruction above before cutting or serving. Serve the finished dish as directed; allow hot portions to cool enough to eat."
    }
  ],
